306. The affix ṅîp is employed, in forming the feminine, after the crude-forms ending in ṛ or in n ;

Thus क्रोष्टु becomes क्रोष्ट्री and is declined as Nom : क्रोष्ट्री ; क्रोष्ट्र्यौ ; क्रोष्ट्र्यः ।

Declension of Feminine nouns ending in û ;

The Feminine Noun वधू is declined like गौरी ; भू is declined like श्री. Its Voc. Sing is हे सुभ्रूः । How then does the Bhaṭṭi use the Voc. Sing as सुभ्रु in the following passage 'हा पितः क्वासि हे सुभ्रु' ? The Bhaṭṭi has misapplied Sûtra I. 2. 48 S. 656 which is not applicable because सुभ्रू is not formed by any Feminine affix but by the affix ‹?› added to the root ‹?› (See Uṇâdi II. 68). If he has not applied that rule, he might have applied the Sûtra VII. 3. 107. S. 267

454. The affix टाप् is employed to indicate feminine nature, after the crude-forms 'aja' &c, and the crude-forms ending in short a.

This debars ङीष् and ङीप् ।

The words अज &c. are given below. Thus अज a 'he goat,' अजा 'a she goat.' The words ending in short a are such as, खट्वा whose feminine will be खट्वा.

Note:—The word खट्वा is formed by adding the Uṇādi affix ‹?› to the root खट् meaning 'to desire.' (Uṇādi I. 151).

The feminines in grammar do not follow the natural physiological division of sexes, and even names of things which have no sex may have genders, e.g. तटः, तटी, तटम् ॥ Similarly beings whose sexes may be feminines may have names whose Genders will be masculines, such as दाराः ॥

The words अज &c, must denote by themselves a feminine object in order to get the affix टाप्, therefore not in पञ्चाजी meaning 'a collection of five goats'. Here the feminine nature does not refer to the goats, but to the compound noun formed of पञ्च and अज. Therefore this feminine पञ्चाजी is formed by ङीप् (IV. 1. 21. S. 479).

Following are the words belonging to the अजादि class :
1. अज, अजा ;
2. एडक, एडका ;
(3. कोकिल, कोकिला) ;
4. चटक, चटका ;
5. अश्व, अश्वा ;
6. मूषिक, मूषिका ;

Note:—The above words denote 'jāti' or kind and though they end in short a in the masculine, they would have taken, but for the present sûtra, the affix 'ñīṣ' (IV. 1. 63. S. 518) in the feminine.

7. बाल, बाला ;
8. होड, होडा ;
(9. पाक, पाका) ;
10. वत्स, वत्सा ;
11. मन्द, मन्दा ;
12. विलात, विलाता ;

Note:—The above six words are descriptive of age, and though they end in short a in the masculine, but for the present sûtra, they would have taken the affix 'ṅīp' (IV. 1. 20. S. 478) in the feminine.

13. पूर्वापवापण, पूर्वापवापणा ;
14. अपरापवापण, अपरापवापणा ;

Note:—These two words are formed by the affix lyuṭ, and being tit, would have taken ṅīp (IV. 1. 15. S. 470) but for this Sûtra.

Vartika:—The words सं, भद्र, अजिन, शण and पिण्ड when followed by फल form the feminines with टाप् ।

15. संफल, संफला ;
16. भद्रफल, भद्रफला ;
17. अजिनफल, अजिनफला ;
18. शणफल, शणफला ;
19. पिण्डफल, पिण्डफला ;
(20. त्रिफल, त्रिफला ;) ;

In फला, the long ā of phala is changed to short a by the sûtra VI. 3. S. 1001.

Note:—The above words ending in 'phala' would have taken the affix ñīṣ (IV. 1. 64. S. 519) but for their enumeration in the 'ajādi' class; 'त्रिफला' when a Dvigu Compound forms its feminine as त्रिफला ; when a Bahuvrīhi Compound, its feminine is त्रिफली ॥

Vartika:—The word पुष्प preceded by सत्, अच्, काण्ड, प्रान्त and शत takes the affix टाप् ॥

21. सत्पुष्प, सत्पुष्पा ;
22. प्राक्पुष्प, प्राक्पुष्पा ; So also प्रत्यक्पुष्पा
23. काण्डपुष्प, काण्डपुष्पा ;
24. प्रान्तपुष्प, प्रान्तपुष्पा ;
25. शतपुष्प, शतपुष्पा ;
26. एकपुष्प, एकपुष्पा ;

The above words ending in पुष्प would have taken ñīṣ by IV. 1. 64. S. 519.
